! h-fcc-magnon.in in a uniform field along the moment, B_field(3) = 0.02 Ry:
! the Larmor case of the transverse spin susceptibility (notes/incompat/I58.md).
!
! The field enters the potential as -B on the up channel (E = -int B.m), so a
! majority-up moment is parallel to it and the uniform precession sits at the
! Zeeman energy 2 B = 0.04 Ry (544 meV) rather than at zero, below the Stoner
! onset of this cell (0.146 Ry at zero field, the smallest eps_dn - eps_up of
! an empty minority and an occupied majority state at one k).
!
! The field is this large on purpose. On this 4x4x4 mesh no eigenvalue lies
! within a few degauss of the Fermi level, so at B = 0.002 the bands only shift
! rigidly (up by -B, down by +B, m moved by 2e-6) and the field run is the
! zero-field run relabelled, which is a check of the sign and nothing more. At
! 0.02 levels cross the Fermi level and the moment answers the field. Everything else is h-fcc-magnon.in, seed included,
! and that file's header says why the seed is 0.9 and not 1.0.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 6.5,
    nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.01,
    nspin = 2
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.9
    B_field(3) = 0.02
    nbnd = 8
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS {automatic}
 4 4 4 0 0 0
